   <widget class="QTextBrowser" name="knn_descrip">
    <property name="geometry">
     <rect>
      <x>30</x>
      <y>80</y>
      <width>981</width>
      <height>301</height>
     </rect>
    </property>
    <property name="html">
     <string>&lt;!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC &quot;-//W3C//DTD HTML 4.0//EN&quot; &quot;http://www.w3.org/TR/REC-html40/strict.dtd&quot;&gt;
&lt;html&gt;&lt;head&gt;&lt;meta name=&quot;qrichtext&quot; content=&quot;1&quot; /&gt;&lt;style type=&quot;text/css&quot;&gt;
p, li { white-space: pre-wrap; }
&lt;/style&gt;&lt;/head&gt;&lt;body style=&quot; font-family:'MS Shell Dlg 2'; font-size:7.8pt; font-weight:400; font-style:normal;&quot;&gt;
&lt;p align=&quot;justify&quot; style=&quot; margin-top:12px; margin-bottom:12px; margin-left:0px; margin-right:0px; -qt-block-indent:0; text-indent:0px;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; font-size:10pt;&quot;&gt;This method considers the distance to the &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; font-size:10pt; font-weight:600;&quot;&gt;K nearest neighbors&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; font-size:10pt;&quot;&gt; and uses &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; font-size:10pt; font-weight:600;&quot;&gt;soft voting&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; font-size:10pt;&quot;&gt;, meaning that closer neighbors carry more weight in determining the final class. It is based on the assumption that nearby buildings are more likely to share similar characteristics and applies &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; font-size:10pt; font-weight:600;&quot;&gt;inverse kernel weighting&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; font-size:10pt;&quot;&gt; to reflect this relationship.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p align=&quot;justify&quot; style=&quot; margin-top:12px; margin-bottom:12px; margin-left:0px; margin-right:0px; -qt-block-indent:0; text-indent:0px;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; font-size:10pt;&quot;&gt;The process begins with an &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; font-size:10pt; font-weight:600;&quot;&gt;initial sample representing 10% of the population&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; font-size:10pt;&quot;&gt;. Building information can be provided either by uploading a CSV file or by using the built-in &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; font-size:10pt; font-weight:600;&quot;&gt;deep learning model&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; font-size:10pt;&quot;&gt; integrated into the tool.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p align=&quot;justify&quot; style=&quot; margin-top:12px; margin-bottom:12px; margin-left:0px; margin-right:0px; -qt-block-indent:0; text-indent:0px;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; font-size:10pt; font-weight:600;&quot;&gt;Convergence&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; font-size:10pt;&quot;&gt; is evaluated based on the stability of the variable of interest—in this case, &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; font-size:10pt; font-weight:600;&quot;&gt;building taxonomies&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; font-size:10pt;&quot;&gt;. If the distribution of taxonomies changes by no more than &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; font-size:10pt; font-weight:600;&quot;&gt;5%&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; font-size:10pt;&quot;&gt; in the subsequent iteration, convergence is assumed. Otherwise, the sample size is incrementally increased by &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; font-size:10pt; font-weight:600;&quot;&gt;5%&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; font-size:10pt;&quot;&gt; in each iteration (e.g., 1st iteration = 10%, 2nd iteration = 15%, and so on) until convergence is reached.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p align=&quot;justify&quot; style=&quot; margin-top:12px; margin-bottom:12px; margin-left:0px; margin-right:0px; -qt-block-indent:0; text-indent:0px;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; font-size:10pt;&quot;&gt;Once convergence is achieved, the &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; font-size:10pt; font-weight:600;&quot;&gt;sampling stage is complete&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; font-size:10pt;&quot;&gt;, and the &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; font-size:10pt; font-weight:600;&quot;&gt;extrapolation process&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; font-size:10pt;&quot;&gt; begins. At this stage, the tool analyzes the buildings of interest, calculates the &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; font-size:10pt; font-weight:600;&quot;&gt;geodesic distance&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; font-size:10pt;&quot;&gt; to all available sampled buildings, and selects the 10 closest ones to estimate a &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; font-size:10pt; font-weight:600;&quot;&gt;probabilistic distribution of likely taxonomies&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; font-size:10pt;&quot;&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/body&gt;&lt;/html&gt;</string>
    </property>
   </widget>
   <widget class="QLabel" name="backg_2">
